# Reggie James

> Reggie James is a UK business adviser and operator, based in Guildford, Surrey, and London, who helps CEOs, founders, boards and investors make the decisions that shape a business. His positioning: "The right decisions change everything. I help business leaders make them."

He brings 25 years of operating experience in technology markets: founding Digital Clarity in 2002, building DC Storm through to its acquisition by Rakuten, leading commercial operations for an internet business listed in Singapore, and serving since 2011 as COO and Executive Director of DBMM Group Inc. (OTC: DBMM), the US public company that owns Digital Clarity.

## Ways to work with him

- The CEO's Commercial Adviser: monthly advisory for founders and CEOs on growth, priorities, positioning, investment and execution.
- The Growth and Performance Review: a fixed-fee independent review of the commercial model, with board-level recommendations.
- The Investor's Commercial Partner: pre-investment commercial assessment and post-investment support for portfolio companies.
- The Next Chapter: strategic projects for businesses changing direction, with optional fractional executive involvement.

Digital Clarity, his firm, delivers commercial growth programmes when a team is needed.

## Key facts

- Founder and Managing Director, Digital Clarity (since 2002). Grew it to 25 to 30 people and more than 200 clients, including Adobe, Xerox and Bentley Systems.
- Built DC Storm, a marketing measurement platform used by around 48% of major media planning and buying agencies before its acquisition by Rakuten.
- COO, Senior Vice President and Executive Director, DBMM Group Inc. (OTC: DBMM), since 2011.
- Earlier: AltaVista global sales; a senior commercial role at a Singapore internet business that listed on SIMEX and was acquired; technology publishing at VNU and Ziff Davis.
- Selected client results: software ARR from $8m to $23m in three years; 88% EMEA revenue growth in 12 months with a 37.6% lower cost per acquisition; 30% more qualified demo requests year on year.
- Host of the Reggie James - Perspectives podcast.

